## 1. Relationship overview (text ERD)

`1` = exactly one; `0..1` = optional one; `0..N` = zero or many.
A child FK row always points to one parent unless the FK is explicitly nullable.

```text
publishers (1) -------- (0..N) books

books (1) ------------ (0..N) book_authors (0..N) ------------ (1) authors
         books <---------------- M:N ----------------> authors

books (1) ------------ (0..N) book_categories (0..N) --------- (1) categories
         books <---------------- M:N ----------------> categories

categories [parent] (0..1) ---- (0..N) categories [child]
                             parent_category_id

customers (1) -------- (0..N) orders
orders (1) ----------- (0..N) order_items (0..N) ------------- (1) books
         orders <--------------- M:N ----------------> books

customers (1) -------- (0..N) reviews (0..N) ----------------- (1) books
```

A book may have multiple authors and multiple categories; neither is encoded as
a list in a single column. A catalog draft may initially have no associations;
all sample books have at least one author and one category. Each junction row
contains exactly one valid key from each endpoint. The two junction PKs prohibit
duplicates. `order_items` additionally records quantity and the sale price.
There is no 1:1 relationship required by this design.

