## 8. Running the matching SQL

Open phpMyAdmin, select `bookstore_db`, and import `bookstore_db.sql` with UTF-8 encoding.
On a fresh server, first create an empty `bookstore_db` database with utf8mb4_unicode_ci. The script creates
`bookstore_db`, ten base tables, two views, all sample records and final checks.
Re-importing resets these homework tables and views, so back up edits first.
It never drops another database. The final SELECT statements check row counts and order totals; phpMyAdmin may
show only its import-success banner. Browse the tables/views to inspect the data.
Keep this database for Homework 7.
